        "original_id": "31a8d536-0890-57cf-9150-4e7e270c2077",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tom Dey, Alfred Gough, Miles Millar, Roger Yuan, Jackie Chan, Chow Yun-fat\n- Works: Shanghai Noon, Showtime, Failure to Launch, Marmaduke, Bulletproof Monk, Batman Begins, Skyfall\n- Roles: film director, screenwriter, producer, actor\n\nFacts:\n- Tom Dey was born on April 14, 1965, and he is an American film director, screenwriter, and producer.\n- Shanghai Noon marked Tom Dey's directorial debut.\n- Alfred Gough and Miles Millar wrote Shanghai Noon.\n- In 2000, Roger Yuan appeared in Shanghai Noon opposite Jackie Chan.\n- Tom Dey's credits include Shanghai Noon, Showtime, Failure to Launch, and Marmaduke.\n- In 2003, Roger Yuan appeared in Bulletproof Monk alongside Chow Yun-fat.\n- In 2005, Roger Yuan appeared as the technician in Batman Begins.\n- In 2012, Roger Yuan appeared as Severine's bodyguard in Skyfall.",
